A main-actor, reference-counted idle-timer holder, so one screen's onDisappear can't undo another's onAppear while the shared cover swaps them:

```swift
import UIKit

/// Keeps the display awake while the lyrics screen or the sync editor is visible (owner request 2026-10: always on).
enum ScreenAwake {
    private static var holders = Set<String>()
    static func hold(_ id: String) { holders.insert(id); apply() }
    static func release(_ id: String) { holders.remove(id); apply() }
    private static func apply() { UIApplication.shared.isIdleTimerDisabled = !holders.isEmpty }
}
```

- The app target's default isolation is MainActor (project.yml:60), so the static stored var is main-actor isolated and compiles under Swift 6 strict concurrency. Precedent: the static vars at LyricsSyncEditorView.swift:32-34.
- hold() is idempotent, so it can be called again to re-assert.
